 CrOS customizations to 225-r1  This applies our customizations that still matter:  - put sys-fs/udev-init-scripts behind USE=openrc  - drop the lvm2 blocker as we build/run fine w/out it  - rename /lib/systemd/systemd-udevd back to /sbin/udevd  BUG=chrome-os-partner:59259 TEST=pre-cq passes  Change-Id: I58fa7ddf36bee229a22edc7eda8c299613635a05 Signed-off-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/406672 Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="406672" owner_email="mka@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/72/406672/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie0c33a7727408a41516764215d66f7dbee20492d" commit="aa74c57f571c1f1e50e7f14e46e58c0d769c61d9" commit_message="[autotest] Increase MySQL connection timeout  Increasing the connection timeout should make initial connection errors less likely.  The default value seems to be 10 seconds (in MySQL documentation), but I think this depends on how the underlying MySQL C library was compiled. The logs in the bug suggest a timeout of ~5 seconds.  Also, increase the overall timeout to 4 minutes to compensate for the increased per-try timeout.  One concern is that if this is called in an RPC, the RPC response will timeout before this connection attempt. However, the existing 2 minute timeout already rules out this case.  BUG=chromium:660520 TEST=None  Change-Id: Ie0c33a7727408a41516764215d66f7dbee20492d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/405829 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Allen Li &lt;ayatane@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="405829" owner_email="ayatane@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/29/405829/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If35d8bfc4b2c7f2ea90173efb1baf16a79407801" commit="6028148d8f98d037820a7c834227a315443a2cc4" commit_message="[autotest] Translate board name in build target for certain Android boards  This is to support certain Android boards that use different board name in build target.  BUG=b:32579855 TEST=local run, unittest /usr/local/autotest/site_utils/suite_scheduler/suite_scheduler.py \       -d /usr/local/autotest/logs -f /usr/local/autotest/dshi/test_ss_2.ini  \       -e nightly -i git_nyc-mr1-release/seed_l8150-userdebug/3405385  \       -r /tmp/_autotmp_0pjXWQ_suite_scheduler -o android  $ cat dshi/test_ss_2.ini [Android_Bluetooth_Nightly_Seed] run_on: nightly hour: 4 suite: android_bluetooth os_type: android branches: git_nyc-mr1-release boards: gm4g_sprout-2 targets: seed_l8150-userdebug pool: suites no_delay: True  also make sure boards doesn't need the mapping still works.  Change-Id: If35d8bfc4b2c7f2ea90173efb1baf16a79407801 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/407845 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Kris Rambish &lt;krisr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="407845" owner_email="dshi@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/45/407845/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If5f8487472f1092b5ebc24e3df90c7965aa382d0" commit="b17044b85dfe584d7990d3694277267c4eea173a" commit_message="[autotest] Loosens board list check when adding new board labels.  testbed may have a mix of different boards. This change loosens the board list check to allow any board labels ending with -number to be added to a host.  BUG=chromium:660271 TEST=unittest  Change-Id: If5f8487472f1092b5ebc24e3df90c7965aa382d0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/407068 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="407068" owner_email="dshi@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/68/407068/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2fc0975d85dd3d81591d6cc58cf303f84898fbbd" commit="ee418b2f4a59e35fd7bb572eb2cb797c10ce8975" commit_message="power: Add TABLET_MODE_UNSUPPORTED state.  powerd's TabletMode enum previously just had TABLET_MODE_ON and TABLET_MODE_OFF values. While tablet mode is arguably &quot;off&quot; on non-convertible devices that don't have tablet mode switches, using TABLET_MODE_OFF here results in confusing logging. Introduce a new TABLET_MODE_UNSUPPORTED value for these devices.  Also clean up some test code to handle tri-state enums more cleanly instead of aborting on unexpected values.  BUG=none TEST=updated tests; also confirmed that confusing &quot;Exited      tablet mode&quot; message is no longer logged at boot on      samus  Change-Id: I2fc0975d85dd3d81591d6cc58cf303f84898fbbd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/406567 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Eric Caruso &lt;ejcaruso@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="406567" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/67/406567/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0db540e36e3326fc463251a9ce421519146c55f0" commit="aee85821303f7959155faebd5949d408348320b8" commit_message="power: Log a message when lid is closed at startup.  Make powerd log &quot;Lid closed at startup&quot; if the lid is... well, closed at startup. We already log lid state changes, so this makes it easier to figure out what's going on if the system reboots while the lid is closed.  BUG=none TEST=manual: booted system and quickly closed lid; message      was written to log  Change-Id: I0db540e36e3326fc463251a9ce421519146c55f0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/405695 Commit-Ready: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="8" gerrit_number="405695" owner_email="derat@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/95/405695/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="8"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iabfecb75bcbedf4b28df3e56d17da827af389c97" commit="3e358b77dc0ae0d9cb32a550304159a6d8a06bd9" commit_message="hostapd: ctrl interface channel change error logging  Add logging information when channel change fails  BUG=b:32604427 TEST=manually on gale  Change-Id: Iabfecb75bcbedf4b28df3e56d17da827af389c97 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/406483 Commit-Ready: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Zhihong Yu &lt;zhihongyu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="4" gerrit_number="406483" owner_email="julanhsu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/hostap" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hostap" ref="refs/changes/83/406483/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I15e22269d82d32814edc9725c46065fc1bc7d86b" commit="d4ec72db693000b05ad92ba9f0baaf1f0c36ab81" commit_message="laptop-mode-tools: Refactor usb_autosuspend::listed_by_id  usb_autosuspend's listed_by_id functions is horribly inefficient, it launches dozens of child processes for each USB device. At boot init runs &quot;laptop-mode force&quot;, which can take 20+ seconds (on kevin). This combined with usb_autosuspend udev handlers which are slow for the same reason can cause other udev handlers to timeout and devices being available too late. This patch refactors listed_by_id which reduces the execution time of usb_autosuspend by factor 10+.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:58864 TEST=boot kevin with Gnubby attached   USB_DEV=$(dmesg | grep gnubby | sed -e &quot;s/.*\(.-1\):.*/\1/&quot;)   cat /sys/bus/usb/devices/${USB_DEV}/power/control     =&gt; auto   manual tests with debug logs show significant reduction in runtime  Change-Id: I15e22269d82d32814edc9725c46065fc1bc7d86b Signed-off-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/407517 Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="407517" owner_email="mka@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/17/407517/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I0bdd17d4e1db42bad51769801d585f091127c629" commit="25fa465fac7086ef1f4f978f4b1da5580194388f" commit_message="[autotest] Change suite_scheduler.ini to be deployed by puppet  This way we don't need a push to prod to update suite_scheduler.ini change.  BUG=b:31860543 TEST=None  Change-Id: I0bdd17d4e1db42bad51769801d585f091127c629 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/407439 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="407439" owner_email="dshi@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/39/407439/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><lkgm version="8960.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>